Note: ===== Audio Effects (DSP) =====

Note: Apply Schroeder reverb with room size (0-1), default damping and mix
internal proc reverb(Buffer: buffer, Double: roomSize)

Note: Apply Schroeder reverb with room size (0-1), damping (0-1), and wet/dry mix (0-1)
internal proc reverb(Buffer: buffer, Double: roomSize, Double: damping, Double: mix)

Note: Apply lowpass filter at cutoff frequency (Hz)
internal proc lowpass(Buffer: buffer, Double: cutoffHz)

Note: Apply highpass filter at cutoff frequency (Hz)
internal proc highpass(Buffer: buffer, Double: cutoffHz)

Note: Apply bandpass filter between low and high frequencies (Hz)
internal proc bandpass(Buffer: buffer, Double: lowHz, Double: highHz)

Note: Apply dynamic range compression with threshold (dB, must be <= 0) and ratio (>= 1.0)
internal proc compress(Buffer: buffer, Double: thresholdDb, Double: ratio)

Note: Apply compression with full control: threshold (dB), ratio, attack (ms), release (ms)
internal proc compress(Buffer: buffer, Double: thresholdDb, Double: ratio, Double: attackMs, Double: releaseMs)

Note: Apply feedback delay with time (ms), feedback (0-1), and wet/dry mix (0-1)
internal proc delay(Buffer: buffer, Double: delayMs, Double: feedback, Double: mix)

Note: Tempo-synced feedback delay; rate is a NoteValue (EIGHTH, QUARTER, ...) read against the active MusicalContext.Tempo
internal proc delay(Buffer: buffer, NoteValue: rate, Double: feedback, Double: mix)

Note: Apply gain in dB (negative = attenuate, positive = amplify). Returns new buffer.
internal proc gain(Buffer: buffer, Double: gainDb)

Note: Explicit dB ergonomics; same dB semantics as the bare-Double gain overload above.
internal proc gain(Buffer: buffer, Decibel: gainDb)

Note: volume(Buffer, Double linear) — linear-multiplier alternative to gain(dB).
Note: gain treats arg as decibels, volume treats arg as a bare linear multiplier (0.5 = half).
internal proc volume(Buffer: buffer, Double: linearMultiplier)

Note: Apply sidechain compression: source ducks under trigger signal
internal proc sidechain(Buffer: source, Buffer: trigger, Double: thresholdDb, Double: ratio)

Note: Apply sidechain compression with custom attack and release times (ms)
internal proc sidechain(Buffer: source, Buffer: trigger, Double: thresholdDb, Double: ratio, Double: attackMs, Double: releaseMs)

Note: Apply constant-power stereo panning. Pan: -1.0 = left, 0.0 = center, 1.0 = right. Returns stereo buffer.
internal proc pan(Buffer: buffer, Double: panValue)

Note: ===== Music-type FX overloads =====
Note: Each line below surfaces a C# overload registered in EffectsFunctions.cs. Without
Note: a matching internal proc forward decl the C# registration is invisible to user
Note: code. Same DSP path as the bare-Double overload above each pair.

Note: delay(Buffer, Millisecond, ...) — explicit ms ergonomics
internal proc delay(Buffer: buffer, Millisecond: delayMs, Double: feedback, Double: mix)

Note: delay(Buffer, Beat, ...) -- tempo-synced rate in beats; reads MusicalContext.Tempo (default 120 BPM + one-shot advisory)
internal proc delay(Buffer: buffer, Beat: beats, Double: feedback, Double: mix)

Note: compress(Buffer, Decibel threshold, ratio, Millisecond attack, Millisecond release) — full music-typed
internal proc compress(Buffer: buffer, Decibel: thresholdDb, Double: ratio, Millisecond: attackMs, Millisecond: releaseMs)

Note: sidechain(Buffer source, Buffer trigger, Decibel threshold, ratio, Millisecond attack, Millisecond release)
internal proc sidechain(Buffer: source, Buffer: trigger, Decibel: thresholdDb, Double: ratio, Millisecond: attackMs, Millisecond: releaseMs)

Note: reverb(Buffer, Double mix, Second decay) — decay time as Second (typical 0.3s-3.0s)
internal proc reverb(Buffer: buffer, Double: roomSize, Second: decaySec)

Note: lowpass / highpass / bandpass with Hertz cutoff — explicit frequency-type ergonomics
internal proc lowpass(Buffer: buffer, Hertz: cutoffHz)
internal proc highpass(Buffer: buffer, Hertz: cutoffHz)
internal proc bandpass(Buffer: buffer, Hertz: lowHz, Hertz: highHz)

